                <pb facs="0268" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/1023: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McCafferty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-13T17:00:00-07:00">December 13, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>102. The political situation has now improved considerably and the new Government
                    seems to have complete control of the situation. At the present there does not
                    seem to be danger of any outbreak or unrest in the immediate future.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McCafferty</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
